Module overexall "Over Exall" {
  Milestone oe_ms_back "walked on the Lodger's back" worth 80 when been(party, back).
  Milestone oe_ms_answer "heard the Lodger answer the bell" worth 40 when knows(party, answer_heard).
  Milestone oe_ms_barbel "watched the Lodger take a hide at night" worth 40 when knows(party, barbel_known).
  Milestone oe_ms_leaven "learned whose bread the Old Leaven is" worth 60 when knows(party, leaven_known).
  Milestone oe_ms_iron "found Saley's iron in the Lodger's shoulder" worth 60 when knows(party, iron_known).
  Milestone oe_ms_saley "stayed Saley's gun" worth 100 when saleyHeld(party) or spiked(party).
  Milestone oe_ms_fire "lit the Long Fire" worth 150 when warmed(party).
  Milestone oe_ms_fed "fed the Lodger what it is" worth 150 when fed(party).
  Milestone oe_ms_iron_out "cut the iron out" worth 150 when unburdened(party).
  Milestone oe_ms_dorcas "took Dorcas Holle up" worth 100 when aboard(party).

  Ending arithmetic_dorcas "Arithmetic, and a Handkerchief" over arithmetic when struck(party) and aboard(party)
    "The harpoon goes in behind the eye, and the breath that goes out of the Lodger is very long. On the shoulder Dorcas Holle has time to say, quite clearly, 'There, now.' Then it comes down on the Edge, as Saley promised, with enormous gentleness, and lies there with its eye shut. Dorcas is found on the skin in the morning in her good coat, one hand flat on the grey, and a handkerchief in the other. The oil rains on Exall for a month. Saley is paid, and does not collect. Letty Forne rings the hours on the bare bell for the rest of her life, and the bell, in a sky with nothing in it, is not answered.".
  Ending arithmetic "Arithmetic" when struck(party)
    "The Lodger comes down on the Edge, as Saley promised: not on the roofs. It lies there like a hill that has made a mistake. For a month the lamp-oil comes down the High Street in a warm yellow rain, and the town lights its lamps with it for twenty years. Perrin Elley bakes with the grease, and the Skyloaf is not the same. Captain Saley of Cloudgate is seen at dawn on the Windlass Field, sitting by the cold kettle, looking at nothing, and is gone by evening. Marta Hord makes a very great deal of money from the hide.".
  Ending candlemas "Candlemas" when rose() and aboard(party)
    "At dawn the Lodger lets go of the steeple. It does it like a man getting out of a chair, in stages. The rain stops. The belly lifts over the Cross, and Exall, all of it, three hundred and eleven people and a goat, stands in the street with its mouth open and the sun on its face for the first time in four days. On the shoulder, small and upright in a good coat, a very old woman has stood up and is waving a handkerchief. At the foot of the spire Letty Forne takes the felt off the bell, and the fleece, and rings the hour with the clapper bare, and the sky answers her, a third below, all the way up. Nobody in Exall will be believed about this. Perrin Elley will sell a loaf of it for ten coin to anyone who asks.".
  Ending leaves "The Lodger Leaves" when rose()
    "At dawn the Lodger lets go of the steeple. It does it like a man getting out of a chair, in stages. The rain stops. The belly lifts over the Cross, and the whole town stands in the street in the sun with its mouth open. It goes up the ridge, slowly, a grey hill with the light on it, and over the Edge, and into the first of the cloud, which closes behind it. Letty Forne takes the felt off the bell, and the fleece, and rings the hour with the clapper bare. In the quiet after it, a third below, from a great way off, something hums along. Dorcas Holle watches it from her window and says nothing at all. The High Street stays wet for a month, and the children sing about it.".
  Ending stays "The Lodger Stays" when dawn4() and lifted() == 1
    "It does not go. It does not fall, either. It sinks, over a long morning, in a great gentle slither of tile and breath, until it has found the Edge and the ridge and settled over the whole of Exall like a hen. The Tarpaulin has to be rebuilt. Nobody is hurt. By Michaelmas there is a door cut into the whale's flank at the Cross, and a warm draught from it, and the town has a ceiling. Exall is the only place in the Brack where it does not rain. The Skyloaf is fed every dawn by a barbel as thick as a mainmast, with enormous delicacy, from a crock on the roof.".
  Ending fall_dorcas "The Roof of the World" over fall when dawn4() and lifted() == 0 and aboard(party)
    "By the fourth morning the Lodger is on the roofs. Dorcas Holle is on the Lodger, in her good coat, with her palm flat on its shoulder, when it goes. She does not seem to mind. The breath goes out of the animal, and the heavy grey weight comes down all along the ridge, and Exall goes under it with a sound like a great many doors being quietly shut. The ridge is a ridge. It has the Lodger's long back on it for a hundred years, and a thousand foxes, and in the spring the brass-coloured moss.".
  Ending fall "The Roof of the World" when dawn4() and lifted() == 0
    "By the fourth morning the Lodger is on the roofs. The breath goes out of it, with something very like relief, and the heavy grey weight comes down all along the ridge, and Exall goes under it with a sound like a great many doors being quietly shut. The ridge is a ridge. It has the Lodger's long back on it for a hundred years, and in the spring there is brass-coloured moss, and in the summer, the pale hats of jelly, drifting up out of the ruins in one direction.".
}
